WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.530
A friend in another city
sends you a short video clip.

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.170
It's chopped into small blocks, and they
scatter across a network of routers.

3
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.690
Some arrive early, some late, all jumbled.

4
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.950
Yet the clip plays perfectly.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.170
So how can it arrive in order, if
its pieces take different routes?

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.790
In this mission, you'll see why data is
broken into small pieces called packets

7
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.350
before it is sent.

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.210
You'll look inside one:
a header with addresses,

9
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.050
and a payload of data.

10
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.930
And you'll watch routers read each packet's
destination address and pass it on.

11
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:39.090
Your mission: explain how a video can arrive
in order when its pieces take different

12
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:39.760
routes.
